@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam Style strictuml
skinparam SequenceMessageAlignment center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam RoundCorner 10

title Pigeon Lab: Phase 2 - Resilient Payment Settlement Architecture

actor "Customer" as User
box "Pigeon Service (Spring Boot 3.x / Java 21)" #F0F8FF
    participant "PaymentController" as API
    participant "KafkaProducer" as Prod
    participant "KafkaConsumer" as Cons
    participant "S3Service" as S3S
end box

queue "Kafka Bus (KRaft)" as Kafka #Yellow
database "AWS S3 (Hyderabad)" as AWS #Orange
database "Postgres Ledger" as DB #LightGreen

== PHASE 1: ASYNCHRONOUS INGRESS ==
note over User, Kafka: Goal: High Availability & Low Latency
User -> API : POST /api/payments
note right: Validates Request Schema

API -> Prod : dispatch(PaymentTxn)
Prod -> Kafka : Publish Topic: 'payment-transactions-v1'
Kafka --> Prod : Broker Ack
Prod --> API : Success
API --> User : **202 Accepted**
note left: User is released immediately. \nKafka handles the "Pigeon".

== PHASE 2: RESILIENT SETTLEMENT ==
note over Kafka, DB: Goal: Zero Data Loss & Auditability
Kafka -> Cons : Poll Message
note right: Triggered by **Virtual Threads**

Cons -> DB : Guard 1: Idempotency Check
DB --> Cons : Result: New Transaction

group #FFEBEE [CRITICAL AUDIT FORTRESS]
    Cons -> S3S : uploadFile(receipt_bytes)
    S3S -> AWS : **PutObject** (ap-south-2)
    note right: Store evidence in Region closest to Bank
    AWS --> S3S : s3_evidence_key (Audit Reference)

    Cons -> DB : Guard 2: Atomic Save(Entity + S3_Key)
    DB --> Cons : **Fortified (Commit)**
end

Cons -> Kafka : **ack.acknowledge()**
note over Kafka, Cons: **Manual Ack Strategy:** \nOffset only moves IF S3 and DB succeed. \nThis prevents "ghost" payments.

footer Pigeon Lab Phase 2 - Sachin (Targeting Lloyds Bank Standards)
@enduml
